-- Sandhyavandanam, book pages 16 to 27: from the achamanam to the seal the book
-- puts on its own first half. Eighteen steps.
--
-- Source: Yajurveda Trikaala Sandhyaavandanam, Giri Trading Agency, English
-- translation by A. R. Parthasarathi. Mantras transcribed from photographs of
-- the printed page; the English here is written for this app, because the
-- book's glosses and rubrics are the editor's prose.
--
-- THREE SITTINGS, THREE KINDS OF DIFFERENCE, and the data follows the rite
-- rather than one convenient pattern:
--
--   different mantra, same action -> three rows, one mode each. The Sankalpa,
--   and the Prashanam, which is three entirely separate mantras.
--
--   same mantra, different count -> one row, the count in instruction_en.
--   Arghyam is offered three times morning and evening, twice at noon.
--
--   same everything -> one row carrying all three modes.
--
-- THREE MISPRINTS ARE CORRECTED, each with its evidence:
--
--   यो वशिशवतमो रसः  ->  यो वः शिवतमो रसः
--   Book pages 21 and 24 both set यो वशिशवतमो रसः -- the visarga after वः
--   lost and शि doubled. Three readings agree against the page: this book's
--   OWN roman four lines below ("yo vah-shivatamo rasaha"), the Bhavan
--   edition's roman ("yo vah sivatamorasah"), and the received text of the
--   Rigvedic apo hi shtha. The same wrong setting appears twice with the
--   right roman twice, which means reused type rather than a compositor
--   slipping.
--
--   ओं भूर्भुवस्तुवः।  ->  ओं भूर्भुवः सुवः।
--   Book page 25 sets तुवः where the roman beside it reads "suvaha" and
--   every other occurrence in the book reads सुवः. A स set as त.
--
--   त्रिविक्रमं तर्पयामिा  ->  त्रिविक्रमं तर्पयामि
--   Book page 27 carries a stray aa-matra on one of twenty-one otherwise
--   identical lines. Every other line is तर्पयामि and the roman reads
--   "trivikramam tarpayaami".
--
-- The generator asserts each correction applied exactly as often as expected,
-- so a fix that silently matched nothing fails the build instead of shipping
-- the misprint.
--
-- The pooja stays PLANNED. It is published by 0049, when the japa half lands
-- and the rite is whole.
-- =============================================================================

