values
  ('sandhyavandanam', 9, 'purvangam', 'Marjanam', 'மார்ஜனம்',
   'Sprinkle water over the head with the ring finger at each of the first seven lines. Touch the right and left thighs at the eighth. Sprinkle again at the ninth. Then take water in the right palm and pass it clockwise around the head.',
   'ओं आपो हि ष्ठा मयोभुवः। ता न ऊर्जे दधातन।
महे रणाय चक्षसे। यो वः शिवतमो रसः। तस्य भाजयतेह नः।
उशतीरिव मातरः। तस्मा अरङ्गमाम वः।
यस्य क्षयाय जिन्वथ।
आपो जनयथा च नः। ओं भूर्भुवःसुवः।',
   'ஓம் ஆபோ ஹி ஷ்டா மயோபுவ꞉। தா ந ஊர்ஜே ததாதந।
மஹே ரணாய சக்ஷஸே। யோ வ꞉ ஶிவதமோ ரஸ꞉। தஸ்ய பாஜயதேஹ ந꞉।
உஶதீரிவ மாதர꞉। தஸ்மா அரங்கமாம வ꞉।
யஸ்ய க்ஷயாய ஜிந்வத।
ஆபோ ஜநயதா ச ந꞉। ஓம் பூர்புவ꞉ஸுவ꞉।',
   'oṃ āpo hi ṣṭhā mayobhuvaḥ। tā na ūrje dadhātana।
mahe raṇāya cakṣase। yo vaḥ śivatamo rasaḥ। tasya bhājayateha naḥ।
uśatīriva mātaraḥ। tasmā araṅgamāma vaḥ।
yasya kṣayāya jinvatha।
āpo janayathā ca naḥ। oṃ bhūrbhuvaḥsuvaḥ।',
   'Waters, you are happiness itself; give us vigour, and the sight of a great gladness. Let us share here in that most kindly essence of yours, like mothers who long for us. We come to you for that whose dwelling you quicken. Waters, beget us anew.',
   'The ten lines are choreography, not layout: the book assigns the first seven to the head, the eighth to the thighs, the ninth to sprinkling again, and the tenth is the closing vyahriti rather than another line of the marjanam. Run together as one mantra the step still recites correctly and stops meaning anything.',
   array['pratah', 'madhyahnika', 'sayam']::text[], 'all', true, 'Yajurveda Trikaala Sandhyaavandanam (Giri), pp.16-27, photographed page');

-- 10. Apaam Prashanam — morning
insert into public.pooja_steps
  (pooja_id, step_number, phase, step_title_en, step_title_ta,
   instruction_en, mantra_sanskrit, mantra_tamil, mantra_translit,
   meaning_en, philosophy_en, modes, gender_rule, scripts_generated, source_ref)
values
  ('sandhyavandanam', 10, 'purvangam', 'Apaam Prashanam — morning', 'அபாம் ப்ராஶனம் — காலை',
   'Take one uddharani of water in the palm, recite, and drink the water at the end.',
   'सूर्यश्च मा मन्युश्च मन्युपतयश्च मन्युकृतेभ्यः।
पापेभ्यो रक्षन्ताम्। यद्रात्रिया पापमाकार्षम्॥
मनसा वाचा हस्ताभ्याम्। पद्भ्यामुदरेण शिश्ञा।
रात्रिस्तदवलुम्पतु। यत् किञ्च दुरितं मयि।
इदमहं माममृतयोनौ। सूर्ये ज्योतिषि जुहोमि स्वाहा॥',
   'ஸூர்யஶ்ச மா மந்யுஶ்ச மந்யுபதயஶ்ச மந்யுக்ருதேப்ய꞉।
பாபேப்யோ ரக்ஷந்தாம்। யத்ராத்ரியா பாபமாகார்ஷம்॥
மநஸா வாசா ஹஸ்தாப்யாம்। பத்ப்யாமுதரேண ஶிஶ்ஞா।
ராத்ரிஸ்ததவலும்பது। யத் கிஞ்ச துரிதம் மயி।
இதமஹம் மாமம்ருதயோநௌ। ஸூர்யே ஜ்யோதிஷி ஜுஹோமி ஸ்வாஹா॥',
   'sūryaśca mā manyuśca manyupatayaśca manyukṛtebhyaḥ।
pāpebhyo rakṣantām। yadrātriyā pāpamākārṣam॥
manasā vācā hastābhyām। padbhyāmudareṇa śiśñā।
rātristadavalumpatu। yat kiñca duritaṃ mayi।
idamahaṃ māmamṛtayonau। sūrye jyotiṣi juhomi svāhā॥',
   'May the Sun, and Anger, and the lords of Anger, guard me from the wrong done out of anger; may the night wipe away whatever wrong I did in the night by mind, speech, hands, feet, belly or sex. I offer myself into the sun, into the light, into the deathless. Svaha.',
   'Not one mantra with a word swapped — three different texts, and reading them together shows why. The morning asks the Sun to absolve what was done BY NIGHT; the evening asks Agni to absolve what was done BY DAY; and each offers itself into a different light, the sun in the morning and the truth in the evening. Each sitting cleans the stretch of time behind it. Noon has neither a night nor a day behind it, only a morning of living, so its mantra is about food eaten and gifts taken instead.',
   array['pratah']::text[], 'all', true, 'Yajurveda Trikaala Sandhyaavandanam (Giri), pp.16-27, photographed page');

-- 11. Apaam Prashanam — noon
insert into public.pooja_steps
  (pooja_id, step_number, phase, step_title_en, step_title_ta,
   instruction_en, mantra_sanskrit, mantra_tamil, mantra_translit,
   meaning_en, philosophy_en, modes, gender_rule, scripts_generated, source_ref)
values
  ('sandhyavandanam', 11, 'purvangam', 'Apaam Prashanam — noon', 'அபாம் ப்ராஶனம் — உச்சி',
   'Take one uddharani of water in the palm, recite, and drink the water at the end.',
   'आपः पुनन्तु पृथिवीं पृथिवी पूता पुनातु माम्।
पुनन्तु ब्रह्मणस्पतिर्ब्रह्म पूता पुनातु माम्॥
यदुच्छिष्टमभोज्यं यद्वा दुश्चरितं मम।
सर्वं पुनन्तु मामापोऽसतां च प्रतिग्रहꣳः स्वाहा॥',
   'ஆப꞉ புநந்து ப்ருதிவீம் ப்ருதிவீ பூதா புநாது மாம்।
புநந்து ப்ரஹ்மணஸ்பதிர்ப்ரஹ்ம பூதா புநாது மாம்॥
யதுச்சிஷ்டமபோஜ்யம் யத்வா துஶ்சரிதம் மம।
ஸர்வம் புநந்து மாமாபோஸதாம் ச ப்ரதிக்ரஹகும்꞉ ஸ்வாஹா॥',
   'āpaḥ punantu pṛthivīṃ pṛthivī pūtā punātu mām।
punantu brahmaṇaspatirbrahma pūtā punātu mām॥
yaducchiṣṭamabhojyaṃ yadvā duścaritaṃ mama।
sarvaṃ punantu māmāpo''satāṃ ca pratigrahagmḥ svāhā॥',
   'May the waters purify the earth, and the purified earth purify me; may Brahmanaspati purify, and the purified Veda purify me. Whatever was left over and not to be eaten, whatever I did wrongly, whatever I took from the undeserving — may the waters purify all of it. Svaha.',
   'Not one mantra with a word swapped — three different texts, and reading them together shows why. The morning asks the Sun to absolve what was done BY NIGHT; the evening asks Agni to absolve what was done BY DAY; and each offers itself into a different light, the sun in the morning and the truth in the evening. Each sitting cleans the stretch of time behind it. Noon has neither a night nor a day behind it, only a morning of living, so its mantra is about food eaten and gifts taken instead.',
   array['madhyahnika']::text[], 'all', true, 'Yajurveda Trikaala Sandhyaavandanam (Giri), pp.16-27, photographed page');

-- 12. Apaam Prashanam — evening
insert into public.pooja_steps
  (pooja_id, step_number, phase, step_title_en, step_title_ta,
   instruction_en, mantra_sanskrit, mantra_tamil, mantra_translit,
   meaning_en, philosophy_en, modes, gender_rule, scripts_generated, source_ref)
values
  ('sandhyavandanam', 12, 'purvangam', 'Apaam Prashanam — evening', 'அபாம் ப்ராஶனம் — மாலை',
   'Take one uddharani of water in the palm, recite, and drink the water at the end.',
   'अग्निश्च मा मन्युश्च मन्युपतयश्च मन्युकृतेभ्यः पापेभ्यो रक्षन्ताम्।
यदह्ना पापमकार्षम्। मनसा वाचा हस्ताभ्याम्।
पद्भ्यामुदरेण शिश्ञा। अहस्तदवलुम्पतु यत् किञ्च दुरितं मयि।
इदमहं माममृतयोनौ। सत्ये ज्योतिषि जुहोमि स्वाहा॥',
   'அக்நிஶ்ச மா மந்யுஶ்ச மந்யுபதயஶ்ச மந்யுக்ருதேப்ய꞉ பாபேப்யோ ரக்ஷந்தாம்।
யதஹ்நா பாபமகார்ஷம்। மநஸா வாசா ஹஸ்தாப்யாம்।
பத்ப்யாமுதரேண ஶிஶ்ஞா। அஹஸ்ததவலும்பது யத் கிஞ்ச துரிதம் மயி।
இதமஹம் மாமம்ருதயோநௌ। ஸத்யே ஜ்யோதிஷி ஜுஹோமி ஸ்வாஹா॥',
   'agniśca mā manyuśca manyupatayaśca manyukṛtebhyaḥ pāpebhyo rakṣantām।
yadahnā pāpamakārṣam। manasā vācā hastābhyām।
padbhyāmudareṇa śiśñā। ahastadavalumpatu yat kiñca duritaṃ mayi।
idamahaṃ māmamṛtayonau। satye jyotiṣi juhomi svāhā॥',
   'May Agni, and Anger, and the lords of Anger, guard me from the wrong done out of anger; may the day wipe away whatever wrong I did in the day by mind, speech, hands, feet, belly or sex. I offer myself into the truth, into the light, into the deathless. Svaha.',
   'Not one mantra with a word swapped — three different texts, and reading them together shows why. The morning asks the Sun to absolve what was done BY NIGHT; the evening asks Agni to absolve what was done BY DAY; and each offers itself into a different light, the sun in the morning and the truth in the evening. Each sitting cleans the stretch of time behind it. Noon has neither a night nor a day behind it, only a morning of living, so its mantra is about food eaten and gifts taken instead.',
   array['sayam']::text[], 'all', true, 'Yajurveda Trikaala Sandhyaavandanam (Giri), pp.16-27, photographed page');

-- 13. Punar Marjanam
insert into public.pooja_steps
  (pooja_id, step_number, phase, step_title_en, step_title_ta,
   instruction_en, mantra_sanskrit, mantra_tamil, mantra_translit,
   meaning_en, philosophy_en, modes, gender_rule, scripts_generated, source_ref)
values
  ('sandhyavandanam', 13, 'purvangam', 'Punar Marjanam', 'புனர் மார்ஜனம்',
   'The same sprinkling as the Marjanam, with four further lines added in front of it and included in the same order.',
   'दधिक्राव्णो अकारिषं।
जिष्णोरश्वस्य वाजिनः।
सुरभि नो मुखा करत्।
प्रण आयूꣳषि तारिषत्॥
आपो हि ष्ठा मयोभुवः।
ता न ऊर्जे दधातन।
महे रणाय चक्षसे।
यो वः शिवतमो रसः।
तस्य भाजयतेह नः।
उशतीरिव मातरः।
तस्मा अरङ्गमाम वः।
यस्य क्षयाय जिन्वथ।
आपो जनयथा च नः।
ओं भूर्भुवःसुवः।',
   'ததிக்ராவ்ணோ அகாரிஷம்।
ஜிஷ்ணோரஶ்வஸ்ய வாஜிந꞉।
ஸுரபி நோ முகா கரத்।
ப்ரண ஆயூகும்ஷி தாரிஷத்॥
ஆபோ ஹி ஷ்டா மயோபுவ꞉।
தா ந ஊர்ஜே ததாதந।
மஹே ரணாய சக்ஷஸே।
யோ வ꞉ ஶிவதமோ ரஸ꞉।
தஸ்ய பாஜயதேஹ ந꞉।
உஶதீரிவ மாதர꞉।
தஸ்மா அரங்கமாம வ꞉।
யஸ்ய க்ஷயாய ஜிந்வத।
ஆபோ ஜநயதா ச ந꞉।
ஓம் பூர்புவ꞉ஸுவ꞉।',
   'dadhikrāvṇo akāriṣaṃ।
jiṣṇoraśvasya vājinaḥ।
surabhi no mukhā karat।
praṇa āyūgmṣi tāriṣat॥
āpo hi ṣṭhā mayobhuvaḥ।
tā na ūrje dadhātana।
mahe raṇāya cakṣase।
yo vaḥ śivatamo rasaḥ।
tasya bhājayateha naḥ।
uśatīriva mātaraḥ।
tasmā araṅgamāma vaḥ।
yasya kṣayāya jinvatha।
āpo janayathā ca naḥ।
oṃ bhūrbhuvaḥsuvaḥ।',
   'I have praised Dadhikravan, the swift victorious horse. May he make our mouths fragrant and lengthen our lives. Then the nine lines of the Marjanam again.',
   'Not a second washing. The book says plainly that only four mantras are new and the other ten are the same, and its own gloss reads the horse as Hayagriva, the swiftest and the ground of all learning. The request is physical and specific — make our mouths fragrant, lengthen our lives — said over the organ that is about to do the reciting.',
   array['pratah', 'madhyahnika', 'sayam']::text[], 'all', true, 'Yajurveda Trikaala Sandhyaavandanam (Giri), pp.16-27, photographed page');

-- 14. Arghya Pradanam
insert into public.pooja_steps
  (pooja_id, step_number, phase, step_title_en, step_title_ta,
   instruction_en, mantra_sanskrit, mantra_tamil, mantra_translit,
   meaning_en, philosophy_en, modes, gender_rule, scripts_generated, source_ref)
values
  ('sandhyavandanam', 14, 'purvangam', 'Arghya Pradanam', 'அர்க்ய ப்ரதானம்',
   'Take water in both cupped hands and let it fall from the fingertips at the end of the mantra. THREE times in the morning and in the evening; TWICE at noon. Then do one pranayama.',
   'ओं भूर्भुवः सुवः।
तत्सवितुर्वरेण्यं भर्गो देवस्य धीमहि।
धियो यो नः प्रचोदयात्।',
   'ஓம் பூர்புவ꞉ ஸுவ꞉।
தத்ஸவிதுர்வரேண்யம் பர்கோ தேவஸ்ய தீமஹி।
தியோ யோ ந꞉ ப்ரசோதயாத்।',
   'oṃ bhūrbhuvaḥ suvaḥ।
tatsaviturvareṇyaṃ bhargo devasya dhīmahi।
dhiyo yo naḥ pracodayāt।',
   'The three worlds are Om. We meditate on the brilliance of that god who impels our thoughts.',
   'The first point in the rite where the sittings differ in the ACTION rather than the words. Everything before this changed its mantra and kept its gesture; here the Gayatri is the same at all three and the count is not. Two at noon and three at either end of the day — the offering is made to the sun at its junctures, and the middle of the day has only one juncture to mark.',
   array['pratah', 'madhyahnika', 'sayam']::text[], 'all', true, 'Yajurveda Trikaala Sandhyaavandanam (Giri), pp.16-27, photographed page');

-- 15. Prayashchitta Arghyam
insert into public.pooja_steps
  (pooja_id, step_number, phase, step_title_en, step_title_ta,
   instruction_en, mantra_sanskrit, mantra_tamil, mantra_translit,
   meaning_en, philosophy_en, modes, gender_rule, scripts_generated, source_ref)
values
  ('sandhyavandanam', 15, 'purvangam', 'Prayashchitta Arghyam', 'ப்ராயஶ்சித்த அர்க்யம்',
   'Hold the hands as for the Sankalpam and recite. Then offer arghyam once more, and pass water around the head reciting the closing line.',
   'कालातीत प्रायश्चित्तार्थम् अर्घ्यप्रदानम् करिष्ये।
ओं भूर्भुवः सुवः।',
   'காலாதீத ப்ராயஶ்சித்தார்தம் அர்க்யப்ரதாநம் கரிஷ்யே।
ஓம் பூர்புவ꞉ ஸுவ꞉।',
   'kālātīta prāyaścittārtham arghyapradānam kariṣye।
oṃ bhūrbhuvaḥ suvaḥ।',
   'For the expiation of the hour having passed, I shall make the offering of arghyam. The three worlds are Om.',
   'This is an apology for being late. Kalatita means the time has gone — the sitting was not kept at its own hour — and the remedy is one extra arghyam offered with a resolution that says so out loud. A rite performed punctually does not need it, and a book that prints it in the ordinary sequence is being realistic about how mornings go.',
   array['pratah', 'madhyahnika', 'sayam']::text[], 'all', true, 'Yajurveda Trikaala Sandhyaavandanam (Giri), pp.16-27, photographed page');

-- 16. Aikyanusandhanam
insert into public.pooja_steps
  (pooja_id, step_number, phase, step_title_en, step_title_ta,
   instruction_en, mantra_sanskrit, mantra_tamil, mantra_translit,
   meaning_en, philosophy_en, modes, gender_rule, scripts_generated, source_ref)
values
  ('sandhyavandanam', 16, 'purvangam', 'Aikyanusandhanam', 'ஐக்யானுஸந்தானம்',
   'Pray silently to Aditya while reciting.',
   'असावादित्यो ब्रह्म-ब्रह्मैवाहमस्मि',
   'அஸாவாதித்யோ ப்ரஹ்ம-ப்ரஹ்மைவாஹமஸ்மி',
   'asāvādityo brahma-brahmaivāhamasmi',
   'That sun is Brahman. I am Brahman.',
   'Eight words, and the book marks them as the life line of the whole sandhyavandanam. Everything before this prepares the reciter; everything after it worships. Here the two are identified, and that is what keeps the rest of the rite from being sun-worship: the arghyam is poured towards the sun, the upasthanam addressed to it, the Gayatri is Savitr''s — and the reciter has just said the sun is Brahman, and so is he.',
   array['pratah', 'madhyahnika', 'sayam']::text[], 'all', true, 'Yajurveda Trikaala Sandhyaavandanam (Giri), pp.16-27, photographed page');

-- 17. Navagraha Deva Tarpanam
insert into public.pooja_steps
  (pooja_id, step_number, phase, step_title_en, step_title_ta,
   instruction_en, mantra_sanskrit, mantra_tamil, mantra_translit,
   meaning_en, philosophy_en, modes, gender_rule, scripts_generated, source_ref)
values
  ('sandhyavandanam', 17, 'purvangam', 'Navagraha Deva Tarpanam', 'நவக்ரஹ தேவ தர்ப்பணம்',
   'Take water in the hand and let it fall from the fingertips once after each name. Do Achamanam and Anga Vandanam once at the end.',
   null,
   null,
   null,
   'Water offered to the nine planets — Sun, Moon, Mars, Mercury, Jupiter, Venus, Saturn, Rahu and Ketu — and then to the twelve names of Narayana, who is Time.',
   'Twenty-one offerings, and the second twelve are the calendar: the book says the Keshava names are Narayana in the form of time, one presiding over each month from Margashirsha to Kartika. So the step waters the planets that govern the sky and then the months that govern the year. These same twelve names have already been touched to the body in the Anga Vandanam; there they were bare and placed on limbs, here they take the accusative and a verb. One list, twice, doing two different things.',
   array['pratah', 'madhyahnika', 'sayam']::text[], 'all', true, 'Yajurveda Trikaala Sandhyaavandanam (Giri), pp.16-27, photographed page');

